1. Difficult Teammate

S: During a college group project, one teammate was not completing their part.
T: We needed to finish the project on time.
A: I talked to them ,  to understood the problem, and helped divide the remaining work.
R: Everyone completed their tasks, and we finished the project on time.

2. Made a Mistake? 

S: During a programming project, I made an error in my code.
T: I needed to fix it before the deadline.
A: I reviewed the code step by step and tested different parts until I found the problem.
R: I fixed the error and learned how to avoid making the same mistake.

3. Worked Under Pressure ? 

S: I once had several assignments and a project due at the same time.
T: I needed to complete everything by the deadlines.
A: I prioritized my work and created a schedule to manage my time.
R: I completed everything on time without sacrificing the quality of my work.

4. Received Feedback ? 

S: A teammate told me that I couldn't  explain my ideas more clearly.
T: I wanted to improve my communication.
A: I listened to the feedback and practiced explaining my ideas in a simpler way.
R: My communication improved, and my teammates understood my ideas better.

5. Learned Something Quickly ? 

S: During a project, I needed to use a technology I had never used before.
T: I needed to learn it quickly to complete my part.
A: I used tutorials, documentation, and practice exercises.
R: I learned the technology and successfully completed my part of the project.

6. Disagreed With a Teammate ? 

S: A teammate and I had different ideas about how to complete a project task.
T: We needed to choose the best approach.
A: I listened to their idea, explained mine, and compared both options.
R: We agreed on the best solution and continued working well together.

7. Multiple Tasks ? 

S: During college, I had several assignments and project tasks at the same time.
T: I needed to manage everything without missing deadlines.
A: I made a task list and prioritized the work based on deadlines.
R: I completed all my assignments and project work on time.

