S: A classmate was having trouble understanding a some concept druing the lecture .
T: I wanted to help them understand it.
A: I explained the concept using a simple example and walked through the code with them.
R: They understood the concept and were able to finish their work.

9. Showed Leadership ? 

S: During a group project, our team was having trouble organizing the work.
T: We needed to make sure everyone knew their responsibilities.
A: I helped divide the tasks and checked our progress regularly.
R: The team became more organized, and we completed the project on time.

10. Solved a Difficult Problem ? 

S: During a programming project, my program was producing an unexpected error.
T: I needed to find the cause and fix it.
A: I tested the code step by step and researched the error when I needed additional information.
R: I found the problem, fixed it, and learned how to troubleshoot similar issues.
